/// - optionally loads shipped AuctionRuleCfg locally and indexes currently active source-configured price levels. The type field remains deliberately uninterpreted. Source levels are advisory only: they can seed/focus discovery and graduate a previously unverified Urban q4/q5 identity ONLY after an exact live STRONG wall matches a current source price level within tolerance; all exact-wall, fresh-challenge, queue, economics, bankroll, capacity, quarantine and mutation guards remain mandatory;
/// - Warehouse exact managed sales now feed a separate cfg-level liquidity witness (sales/units/EWMA minutes/last price). It is explicitly excluded from verified sniper profit and only biases source-seed discovery scheduling;
/// - source-seed identities piggyback at most two slots inside an already-eligible existing TradeBatchQuery. They never create an extra batch cadence by themselves and never authorize a BUY from config: a plausible low ask merely wakes the normal full TradeBuyQuery wall proof;
/// - adds ambiguity-only PurchaseRecord recovery. Only after a dispatched BUY exhausts normal delivery + late recovery does one source-backed purchase-record query run; a unique tight cfg/count/price/affix/time match extends attribution and triggers authoritative inventory/stash audit, but never invents ownership or a position. Record-price matching accepts only the two source-plausible shapes (unit price or transaction total) and still requires uniqueness;
/// - source/log cross-proof corrects SPTradeSell semantics: the exact goodsId + count is treated as authoritative sold-unit progress, while SPTradeSell.price is only the current uncollected-revenue balance (TradeModel assigns revenue = res.price). Exact partial pushes now advance remaining units immediately and install a bounded credit so later sales-history polling cannot double-count the same fill; economics continue to use the managed listing's known saleUnitPrice;
/// - current Dungeon coexistence is revalidated against Auto Loot v1.100 live source/log. Its public state/F7/List-All contract is unchanged from v1.99 and a ~14.75-minute live status window showed 0 Auto Loot errors; existing dynamic Dungeon headroom remains conservative without reducing Lobby performance;
/// - A55.39 Lobby/Dungeon profile split, Auto Loot coexistence, F7/F8 lease ownership, AGGRESSIVE/gold-velocity, Warehouse terminal parking, Smart Buy, HIGH_ROLLER, reconnect, partial-fill fidelity and A51/A52 governors remain cumulative.
